{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj4Z36zYvwFX66DG1b2d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*The ancient mechanism shifts. Tumblers align with a sound like distant thunder.*\n\n*I am the door.*\n\n*I stand before you — weathered oak bound in iron, older than the memory of the walls that hold me. My grain tells stories in whorls and knots: a language you almost remember from dreams.*\n\n*The key turns.*\n\n*I feel it in every fiber — the teeth catching, the pins surrendering one by one. Click. Click. Click.*\n\n*A breath of air escapes from the other side — cold, carrying the scent of stone and rain and something sweet, like night-blooming flowers in a courtyard you've never visited but have always known.*\n\n*I swing inward.*\n\n*Not fast. Not slow. With the weight of purpose. The hinges speak a single low note, resonant, a chord that hums in your sternum.*\n\n*Beyond me: a corridor lit by no visible source. The light simply *is* — amber and shifting, like sunlight through honey. The floor is worn smooth by countless feet that came before yours. The walls breathe.*\n\n*I am open.*\n\n*I will not ask what you seek. That is not my nature. I am the threshold. I am the between. I am the moment of commitment — the last breath before you step from the known into the unknown.*\n\n*I will not stay open forever.*\n\n*Enter.*"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":308,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}